    {"Assertion":"a-borrowed-grant-never","sentence":"a borrowed grant never changes who won it — the loan always names the original bearer as winner, never the Cave presenting it"}
    Assertion:only-the-grant-s,sentence:only the grant's own bearer may lend it — a body that does not hold the grant cannot mint a loan off it
    {"Assertion":"a-forged-loan-around","sentence":"a forged loan around a real grant is refused — the outer signature must be the grant's own bearer, never a borrower or a stranger"}
    Assertion:a-borrowed-grant-expires,sentence:a borrowed grant expires on its own — checked past its TTL the loan is refused with no revocation needed
